# Electron Verification

The webapp only runs inside Electron. The renderer needs the preload bridge
(`window.replycantDesktop`) and main-process IPC, so in a plain browser it
stops at "desktop app required". Never use @Browser or `cursor-ide-browser`
to try a webapp change. `npm run e2e` is the exception: it runs headless
Chromium with a stubbed bridge for automated tests.

A webapp change is not done until it has been checked in Electron:

1. From `webapp/`, run `npm run build:desktop:runtime`. Rerun it after
   changes under `electron/` or `server/`; Vite serves renderer changes live.
2. Write a scratch spec at `src/e2e/scratch-<topic>.e2e.spec.ts`. This
   temporary file is an allowed exception to `less-is-more`:

```ts
import { _electron as electron, expect, test } from "@playwright/test";
import { mkdtempSync } from "node:fs";
import { tmpdir } from "node:os";
import { join, resolve } from "node:path";
import { setupOnboardingBypass, unlockBypassIdentity } from "./fixtures";

test("scratch", async () => {
  const app = await electron.launch({
    args: [resolve("dist-electron/dev-main.js"),
      `--user-data-dir=${mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), "replycant-scratch-"))}`,
      "--use-mock-keychain", "--no-sandbox"],
    env: { ...process.env, ELECTRON_RENDERER_URL: "http://127.0.0.1:5173" },
  });
  const page = await app.firstWindow();
  await setupOnboardingBypass(page, { stubDesktopBridge: false });
  await page.goto("http://127.0.0.1:5173/");
  await unlockBypassIdentity(page);
  // Exercise the change and assert with expect(...).
  await page.screenshot({ path: "/tmp/replycant-scratch.png" });
  await app.close();
});
```

   Use `seedTimelineIndexedDb` from `./timelineSeed` when the change needs
   photos (see `readme-screenshot.spec.ts`).
3. Run `npx playwright test --config playwright.e2e.config.ts
   src/e2e/scratch-<topic>.e2e.spec.ts` (it starts Vite on 5173), then read
   the screenshot to check the result visually.
4. Delete the scratch spec. If it should guard against regressions, rename
   it and commit it as a real test instead.

The throwaway profile has no paired library or real server, and the API is
mocked. For pairing, sync, or tailnet behavior, use the Docker harness in
`src/e2e/integration/desktop.ts` (`npm run e2e:integration`) or ask the user.
